"explanation": "The scientific method relies fundamentally on reproducibility. For a hypothesis to gain widespread scientific acceptance, independent researchers must be able to replicate or duplicate the original experimental results. This process validates the findings, ensuring they are not due to chance, experimental error, or bias. While revising hypotheses, developing theories, and adjusting procedures are part of the broader scientific process, they do not directly validate the initial evidence in the same way that successful replication does.",
